markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Variables</h1>
<p>In the previous level, we observed how computers sort and store data. Let's take a look at how we can declare and define variables in Python.</p>


<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>📖 Variable:</b> A container that stores a value in memory. A variable can only hold one value at a time.</p>
</div>



<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>📖 Data Type:</b> The format of the data that can be stored in a variable.</p>
</div>

## Common Data Types

<div role="list" aria-label="Common Python data types" style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:stretch; gap:16px; width:100%; margin:20px 0; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; box-sizing:border-box;">

  <div role="listitem" style="flex:1 1 170px; min-width:150px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #34BD43; border-radius:4px; overflow:hidden; box-sizing:border-box;">
    <div style="background-color:#CCF1D0; color:#000000; padding:10px; text-align:center; font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:18px; font-weight:700;">boolean</div>
    <div style="min-height:82px; padding:14px 10px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; color:#000000; text-align:center; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">
      <div><span style="font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; color:#000000;">True</span> or <span style="font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; color:#000000;">False</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div role="listitem" style="flex:1 1 170px; min-width:150px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #0099F3; border-radius:4px; overflow:hidden; box-sizing:border-box;">
    <div style="background-color:#D5EFFF; color:#000000; padding:10px; text-align:center; font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:18px; font-weight:700;">int</div>
    <div style="min-height:82px; padding:14px 10px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; color:#000000; text-align:center; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">
      <div><div>Whole numbers,</div><div>like <span style="font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; color:#000000;">7</span> or <span style="font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; color:#000000;">6784</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div role="listitem" style="flex:1 1 170px; min-width:150px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #F46B00; border-radius:4px; overflow:hidden; box-sizing:border-box;">
    <div style="background-color:#FFE3CE; color:#000000; padding:10px; text-align:center; font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:18px; font-weight:700;">float</div>
    <div style="min-height:82px; padding:14px 10px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; color:#000000; text-align:center; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">
      <div><div>Decimal numbers,</div><div>like <span style="font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; color:#000000;">2.5</span> or <span style="font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; color:#000000;">92.81</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div role="listitem" style="flex:1 1 170px; min-width:150px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:4px; overflow:hidden; box-sizing:border-box;">
    <div style="background-color:#E4E2F8; color:#000000; padding:10px; text-align:center; font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:18px; font-weight:700;">String</div>
    <div style="min-height:82px; padding:14px 10px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; color:#000000; text-align:center; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">
      <div><div>A sequence of characters,</div><div>like <span style="font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; color:#000000;">"purple"</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

---
<h2>Creating a Variable</h2>
<p>In Python, you don't have to say what kind of data you're using when you create a variable, Python figures it out for you based on what you type.</p>
<p>For example, if you write <code style = "font-size: 14px;">age = 12</code>, Python knows that age is a number, and if you write <code style = "font-size: 14px;">name = "Alex"</code>, it knows that name is text because of the quotation marks.</p>


<table border="1" width="100%" cellpadding="10">
    <tr>
        <td width="33%">
            <img src="https://images.code.org/4c3ef8ef7dc7363dc0b8ed512ab3836a-image-1727209826025.png" alt="my_score=575" width="100%">
        </td>
        <td width="67%" style="font-size:14pt; padding:18px 22px; line-height:1.6;">
            When we want to create a variable, we write the <b>name</b> we want to use for the information we store.<br><br>We use <b>snake_case</b>, a naming convention where all letters are lowercase and connected with an underscore.
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td width="33%">
            <img src="https://images.code.org/370df57b0518a3aee2e4c9861b45f7a5-image-1727211074412.png" alt="my_score=75" width="100%">
        </td>
        <td width="67%" style="font-size:14pt; padding:18px 22px; line-height:1.6;">
            We use the <b>assignment operator</b> (=) to set or change the value assigned to the variable.
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td width="33%">
            <img src="https://images.code.org/00824a86b12347424b5e6f2cbba0d745-image-1727210984964.png" alt="Image 3" width="100%">
        </td>
        <td width="67%" style="font-size:14pt; padding:18px 22px; line-height:1.6;">
            Then we can specify the <b>starting value</b> to what we want the variable to store.
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

---

<h2>Declaring Different Variable Types</h2>
<p>Variable types are not named when creating variables, however, how you input the value determines the variable type.</p>

<div role="region" aria-label="Python variable examples showing integers, strings, booleans, and floats" style="width:100%; box-sizing:border-box; overflow-x:auto; white-space:nowrap; background-color:#000000; color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:10px; padding:18px 22px; font-family:'Fira Code','Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; line-height:1.7;">
  <span style="color:#FFFFFF;">house_number</span> = <span style="color:#F07FB0;">102</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:#ACA8EA;"># Integer (int)</span><br>
  <span style="color:#FFFFFF;">street_name</span> = <span style="color:#7CDB87;">"Maple Street"</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:#ACA8EA;"># String (str)</span><br>
  <span style="color:#FFFFFF;">resident_name</span> = <span style="color:#7CDB87;">"Sam"</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:#ACA8EA;"># String (str)</span><br>
  <span style="color:#FFFFFF;">has_garden</span> = <span style="color:#6FCAFF;">True</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:#ACA8EA;"># Boolean (bool)</span><br>
  <span style="color:#FFFFFF;">home_price</span> = <span style="color:#F07FB0;">250000.50</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:#ACA8EA;"># Float (float)</span>
</div>
<br>
<h3><b>Notice:</b></h3>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• <b>String</b>, or text, variables are defined using quotation marks.</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• <b>Booleans</b> are defined using the words True or False.</p>

<h2>Let's try creating variables in Python Lab!</h2>
